1
00:00:00,270 --> 00:00:08,708
我敢肯定，你一定有过一些没实现的 App 创意，就是那种在你的笔记应用里躺了两年，
或者你跟朋友喝咖啡时提过的事情。
I'm sure you've had an idea for an app you never built, the kind that stays in your notes app for two years,
or that you mentioned to your friend over a coffee.

2
00:00:08,880 --> 00:00:13,220
就是那种你打开了教程，但一看到技术栈就把它关掉的创意。
The one that you opened up a tutorial for and then closed it as soon as you saw the stack.

3
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:15,428
大多数创意都死在那了。
Most ideas die there.

4
00:00:15,918 --> 00:00:27,172
但 AI 改变了规则。因为从「我想做这个」到「它已经在我的手机上运行」之间的差距，
现在只需要一个周末，而不是六个月。
But AI changed the math. Because the gap between I wanna build this and
it's already running on my phone is now just a weekend and not six months.

5
00:00:27,534 --> 00:00:34,240
你在 YouTube 或 X 上看到的大多数 AI 演示，只
是教你如何在 20 分钟内快速搞出一个玩具项目。
Most AI demos that you see on YouTube or X show you how to spin up a toy project in 20 minutes.

6
00:00:34,510 --> 00:00:40,068
你做完了它，然后试图构建一些真实的东西，结果到第三个功能时整个项目就崩溃了。
You finish it, then try to build something real, and the whole thing falls apart by the third feature.

7
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:44,400
氛围编码无法经受任何严肃项目的考验。
Vibe coding doesn't survive contact with anything serious.

8
00:00:44,654 --> 00:00:46,628
过度工程甚至更糟。
Overengineering is even worse.

9
00:00:46,990 --> 00:00:51,716
花两天时间去规划和编写一个还没任何界面的 App 的架构文档。
Two days of planning and writing architecture docs for an app with zero screens.

10
00:00:52,110 --> 00:00:55,076
这两种方法都会导致最后什么也做不出来。
Both approaches are how nothing gets built.

11
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:57,796
这个视频就在两者之间。
This video sits in the middle.

12
00:00:58,318 --> 00:01:04,196
你将全程使用 AI，在 React Native 中构建一个完整的 Duolingo 克隆应用。
You're gonna build a full Duolingo clone in React Native, using AI the whole way through.

13
00:01:04,750 --> 00:01:16,160
包括新手引导、通过邮件注册和登录、社交认证、语言选择、课程、个人资料，
还有一个你可以真正开口交流的实时 AI 教师。
Onboarding, sign up and sign in with email, plus social auth, language selection, lessons, profile,
and a real-time AI teacher that you can actually talk to out loud.

14
00:01:16,400 --> 00:01:17,680
请跟我重复。
Please repeat after me.

15
00:01:18,030 --> 00:01:19,920
Hola，hola，不错的开始。
Hola, hola, nice start.

16
00:01:20,206 --> 00:01:26,000
你说话，它就来回回应，就像在和一个一直都在的人练习一样。
You speak, it responds back and forth, like practicing with someone who's always around.

17
00:01:26,254 --> 00:01:30,480
试着发一个干净的 O 音，说 hola。
Try hola with a clean O sound, like hola.

18
00:01:32,558 --> 00:01:33,600
这次好多了。
That was much better.

19
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:36,804
你不需要手动写任何一行代码。
You won't write a single line of manual code.

20
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:41,284
你也不会只是盲目地输入提示词然后祈祷它能正常工作。
You also won't just YOLO the prompts and hope it works.

21
00:01:41,902 --> 00:01:45,060
视频的第一部分将教你工作流。
The first part of the video teaches you the workflow.

22
00:01:45,486 --> 00:01:48,452
我把它叫做「实用氛围编程」。
I'm calling it practical vibe coding.

23
00:01:49,230 --> 00:01:56,484
它足够结构化，让你永远不会搞不清代码库里有什么，同时又足够快，让你真的能交付产品。
Structured enough that you never lose track of what's in your code base, but fast enough so that you actually ship.

24
00:01:56,910 --> 00:01:59,044
第二部分是完整的构建过程。
The second part is the full build.

25
00:01:59,790 --> 00:02:00,480
技术栈。
The stack.

26
00:02:00,782 --> 00:02:14,160
React Native 配合 Expo 和 TypeScript，用 NativeWind 做样式，用 Zustand 做状态管理，
用 Clerk 处理身份验证和用户管理，用 Stream 语音智能体驱动实时响应的 AI 教师。
React Native with Expo and TypeScript, NativeWind for styling, Zastant for state management, clerk for auth and user management,
stream voice agents powering the AI teacher that responds in real time.

27
00:02:16,240 --> 00:02:17,680
只需要一点小调整。
Just one small tweak.

28
00:02:17,840 --> 00:02:21,600
10 是带点轻微「是」音的 DS，不是 DS。
10 is DS with a soft yes sound, not DS.

29
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:28,900
用 PostHog 做产品分析，并用 Code Rabbit 在每个 AI 生成的 PR 合并前进行审查。
Post hog for product analytics, and Code Rabbit reviewing every AI generated PR before it merges.

30
00:02:29,774 --> 00:02:32,000
但这个 App 并不是重点。
But the app isn't the point.

31
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:33,360
这个工作流是这样的。
The workflow is.

32
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:43,556
如果你看到视频的后半段，我会向你展示为什么这是利
用 AI 构建移动应用且不陷入那些面条代码的唯一方法。
And if you stick around for the second half, I'll show you why this is the only way
to build mobile applications with AI without getting lost in all that spaghetti code.

33
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:53,636
所以，使用我将在视频中提到的那个工作流，你也可以把它当作参考指南，
我把链接放在描述栏里，把它用在你接下来构建的任何项目上。
So use that workflow that I'll talk about in the video, which you can also get as a reference guide,
I'll leave the link in the description, and use it on anything you build next.

34
00:02:53,934 --> 00:02:58,468
现在，去拿点咖啡、Red Bull 或者茶，我们开始吧。
Now, grab some coffee, Red Bull, or tea, and let's go.

35
00:03:09,200 --> 00:03:18,148
今年早些时候，OpenAI 的创始成员之一 Andre
Karpathy 发布了关于他称之为「氛围编码」的内容。
Earlier this year, Andre Karpathy, one of OpenAI's founding members, posted about something he called vibe coding.

36
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,260
完全交给 AI。
Fully given to AI.

37
00:03:20,654 --> 00:03:24,708
不要读代码，描述你想要什么，然后让它去实现。
Don't read the code, describe what you want, and let it happen.

38
00:03:25,262 --> 00:03:27,280
开发者社区分裂了。
The dev internet split.

39
00:03:27,502 --> 00:03:30,148
一半的回复说这就是未来。
Half the replies said this is the future.

40
00:03:30,414 --> 00:03:34,852
而另一半说这是在构建没人能维护的东西。
And the other half said it's how you build something that nobody can ever maintain.

41
00:03:35,648 --> 00:03:37,412
两种说法都是对的。
Both replies were right.

42
00:03:38,094 --> 00:03:44,036
如果你真的尝试过用纯粹的氛围编码来构建真实的东西，你就知道那是怎么回事了。
If you've actually tried to build something real with pure vibe coding, you know how it goes.

43
00:03:44,528 --> 00:04:00,164
前三个功能飞速完成，然后到第五个功能左右，你让 AI 修复一件事，别的事情就坏了，
你再让它修复，现在你正盯着一段你没写过的代码，在一个你无法完全解释的项目里。
The first three features fly, and then around feature five, you ask AI to fix one thing, something else breaks, you ask it again,
and now you're staring at code that you didn't write in a project you can't fully explain.

44
00:04:00,942 --> 00:04:04,452
没有方向的速度最终都会走到这一步。
Speed without direction always lands here.

45
00:04:04,848 --> 00:04:10,020
但另一种极端看起来完全不同，但最终结果是一样的。
But the other extreme looks completely different, but ends up at the same place.

46
00:04:10,608 --> 00:04:13,860
在任何界面出现之前，先花好几天做规划。
Days of planning before a single screen exists.

47
00:04:14,510 --> 00:04:26,628
文件夹结构、颜色标记、架构文档、命名规范和模式库，为了
让 AI 有可能在某天构建出点什么，而做了数小时的准备工作。
Folder structures, color tokens, architecture docs, naming conventions, and pattern libraries,
hours of prep work for an AI to maybe build something one day.

48
00:04:26,894 --> 00:04:32,128
这感觉很高效，因为你打了很多字，但应用却始终没动工。
It feels productive because you're typing a lot, but the app never gets started.

49
00:04:32,430 --> 00:04:36,356
你本质上是在为一场从未打响的战斗做准备。
You're essentially preparing for a battle without ever fighting one.

50
00:04:36,768 --> 00:04:38,528
那么折中方案是什么？
So what's the middle ground?

51
00:04:38,830 --> 00:04:42,884
这是一种我称之为「实用氛围编程」的方法。
It's a method I call practical vibe coding.

52
00:04:43,470 --> 00:04:52,996
保留 AI 开发的速度，同时加入足够的结构，让 AI 知道它在做什么，而你也不会失去掌控。
Keep the speed of AI development and add just enough structure so that AI knows what it's working on and you don't lose track.

53
00:04:53,454 --> 00:04:58,500
一个功能一个功能地构建，并在进入下一个功能之前验证每一个功能。
Build feature by feature and verify each one before moving to the next.

54
00:04:59,118 --> 00:05:02,404
而这整套方法都运行在一个文件里。
And this whole method runs through one file.

55
00:05:02,766 --> 00:05:08,740
它被称为 agents.md，是项目根目录下的一个 Markdown 文件。
It's called the agents MD, a markdown file at the root of your project.

56
00:05:09,326 --> 00:05:19,844
它告诉 AI 你的项目是如何运作的、你使用的是什么技术栈、文件放在哪里，
以及在你提示词中输入任何内容之前需要遵循哪些规则。
It tells the AI how your project works, what stack you're using, where files
go, and what rules to follow before you say anything else in your prompt.

57
00:05:20,238 --> 00:05:22,084
而且它不是写给你看的。
And it's not written for you.

58
00:05:22,542 --> 00:05:28,484
像 Cursor、Claude Code 和 WindServe 这样的工具会读取项目文件来获取上下文。
Tools like Cursor, Claude Code, and WindServe read project files for context.

59
00:05:28,910 --> 00:05:32,132
而那个 agents.md 文件是它们读取的第一个文件。
And that AgentsMD file is the first file they read.

60
00:05:32,910 --> 00:05:37,668
如果没有它，你最终不得不把同样的上下文内容写进每一个提示词里。
Without it, you'd end up writing the same context lines into every prompt.

61
00:05:38,062 --> 00:05:44,164
同样的技术栈、描述、同样的资料夹规则，还有同样的「用这个，别用那个」。
Same stack, description, same folder rules, same use this and don't use that.

62
00:05:44,750 --> 00:05:49,348
而只要你漏掉其中一项，AI 就会自动填补那个空白。
And the moment you forget to repeat one, the AI fills the gap on its own.

63
00:05:49,774 --> 00:05:55,524
它可能会选择不同的状态库、不同的资料夹惯例，或者不同的样式处理方式。
It picks a different state library, a different folder convention, or a different styling approach.

64
00:05:56,078 --> 00:06:05,892
经过 20 个提示词，你的代码库看起来就像是五个不同的人开
发的，用了 10 种不同的架构模式，而且他们根本没沟通过。
Across 20 prompts, your code base ends up looking like five different people built it
with 10 different architecture patterns who never talk to each other in the first place.

65
00:06:06,574 --> 00:06:10,116
那么 agents.md 文件是由什么组成的呢？
So then what is the agents MD file made of?

66
00:06:10,368 --> 00:06:11,716
首先是角色。
First, a role.

67
00:06:12,462 --> 00:06:15,652
你是一位精通 React Native 加 Expo 的工程师。
You're an expert React Native plus Expo engineer.

68
00:06:16,142 --> 00:06:20,928
你写出干净、简单的代码，你优先考虑清晰度而非抽象化。
You write clean, simple code, you prioritize clarity over abstraction.

69
00:06:21,168 --> 00:06:25,476
仅仅这一段话就能改变后面所有内容的质量。
That paragraph alone changes the quality of everything that follows.

70
00:06:26,350 --> 00:06:32,100
然后给它一个简短的概述：应用是什么、功能是什么，以及谁会使用它。
Then you give it a short overview, what the app is, what does it do, and who uses it.

71
00:06:32,750 --> 00:06:34,084
这里一段话就够了。
One paragraph is enough here.

72
00:06:34,926 --> 00:06:35,780
技术栈。
The stack.

73
00:06:36,238 --> 00:06:40,580
每一个库和服务，每行写出它负责的功能。
Every library and service, one line each on what it handles.

74
00:06:40,974 --> 00:06:44,528
这能防止 AI 在开发过程中推荐其他的替代方案。
This stops the AI from suggesting alternatives mid-build.

75
00:06:44,750 --> 00:06:51,588
还有资料夹结构，包括页面放在哪里、组件放在哪里，还有状态放在哪里。
There's also the folder structure, where screens live, where components go, and where state lives as well.

76
00:06:52,462 --> 00:06:58,528
样式规则，包括你想用的处理方式、颜色标记，或者任何特殊的细节。
The styling rules on what approach you want to use, your color tokens, or any quirks.

77
00:06:58,766 --> 00:07:04,004
例如 Native wind 不支持安全区域视图，就把这点写下来。
Like native wind doesn't work with safe area view, for example, so write that down.

78
00:07:04,238 --> 00:07:06,756
最后是需要遵循的模式。
And finally, the patterns to follow.

79
00:07:07,214 --> 00:07:10,928
任何其他情况下你都必须在不同会话中重复说明的内容。
Anything you'd otherwise have to repeat across different sessions.

80
00:07:11,168 --> 00:07:14,532
而且你不需要一开始就把它写得完美无瑕。
And you don't have to write this perfectly up front.

81
00:07:15,150 --> 00:07:19,524
你先写下你已知的信息，然后在某些问题反覆出现时再更新它。
You write what you know and then update it when something keeps coming up.

82
00:07:20,046 --> 00:07:25,380
比如当 Native wind 在安全区域视图上给我找麻烦时，我就把那个规则加进文件里。
Like when a native wind gave me trouble with safe area view, I added that rule to the file.

83
00:07:25,902 --> 00:07:29,476
在那之后，AI 就再也不犯那个错误了。
And then after that, the AI never made the mistake again.

84
00:07:30,030 --> 00:07:33,796
所以，解决一次，记录下来，然后继续下一步。
So solve it once, document it, and then move on.

85
00:07:34,414 --> 00:07:40,164
现在，这个专案完整的 agents.md 文件是在开发后期才产生的。
Now the fullagents.md file for this project specifically comes later in the build.

86
00:07:40,608 --> 00:07:42,532
它也会放在 GitHub 仓库里。
And it's on the GitHub repo too.

87
00:07:42,928 --> 00:07:53,700
但如果你想要一个可重复使用的模板，你可以把它丢进任何专案中，
配合其他的「实用氛围编程」工作流作为书面参考。
But if you want a reusable template, you can drop into any project and make it work with it,
plus the rest of the practical vibe coding workflow as a written reference.

88
00:07:54,062 --> 00:07:56,804
好，去点击描述栏位里的免费指南。
Well, grab the free playbook linked in the description.

89
00:07:57,198 --> 00:08:01,348
现在让我们多聊聊具体该如何写提示词。
But now let's talk a bit more about how we're gonna actually prompt.

90
00:08:02,030 --> 00:08:05,892
所以，一旦你有了 agents.md 文件，下一步是什么？
So once you've got the agents.md file, what's next?

91
00:08:06,382 --> 00:08:08,132
那具体该怎么用呢？
How do you actually use it?

92
00:08:09,166 --> 00:08:17,008
这个文件负责处理项目上下文，而提示词负责处理你现在正打算构建的内容。
The file handles the project context, but the prompt handles what you're trying to build right now.

93
00:08:17,550 --> 00:08:20,292
这就是我看到大多数开发者搞错的地方。
And this is where I see most developers get it wrong.

94
00:08:20,974 --> 00:08:26,212
他们只写几句想要什么，然后就指望 AI 能把剩下的都搞定。
They type a few sentences about what they want and hope the AI figures out the rest.

95
00:08:26,798 --> 00:08:28,356
有时候确实管用。
Sometimes it works.

96
00:08:28,688 --> 00:08:33,860
但更多时候，输出结果看起来很接近，但又不完全正确。
And more often, the output looks close, but it isn't quite right.

97
00:08:34,048 --> 00:08:41,476
或者它弄坏了原本正常的其他功能，或者我见过它引入了与其余代码库不匹配的模式。
Or it breaks something else that was working, or I've seen it introduce a pattern that doesn't match the rest of the code base.

98
00:08:41,678 --> 00:08:46,148
然后你就得再花 20 分钟去解释哪里出错了。
And then you waste another 20 minutes explaining what went wrong.

99
00:08:47,054 --> 00:08:53,924
所以解决办法不是写更长的提示词，而是结构正确且更具体的提示词。
So the fix isn't a longer prompt, it's a more specific one with the right structure.

100
00:08:54,702 --> 00:09:02,372
因此，我们为这个项目共同编写的每一个提示词都有相同的四个部分，且顺序一致。
So every single prompt that we'll write together for this project has the same four parts and in the same order.

101
00:09:02,894 --> 00:09:07,460
首先是第一点，就是指向你的 agents.md。
Starting with number one, and that is to point it to your agents.md.

102
00:09:08,558 --> 00:09:13,124
可以说类似：先阅读 agents.md 并严格遵守。
Say something like, read the agentsmd first and follow it strictly.

103
00:09:13,614 --> 00:09:15,716
每一次都要这样做，没有任何例外。
Every single time without exceptions.

104
00:09:16,048 --> 00:09:21,380
因为 AI 工具不会自动记住它们在之前的会话中读到的内容。
Because AI tools don't automatically remember what they read in previous sessions.

105
00:09:21,648 --> 00:09:27,364
所以这两行能在任何代码被编写之前，强制把这个文件带入上下文。
So these two lines force the file back into the context before any code gets written.

106
00:09:27,790 --> 00:09:35,088
而且“严格”也很重要，因为它传达出那个文件里的规则不是建议。
And that strictly matters too, because it signals that the rules in that file aren't just suggestions.

107
00:09:35,310 --> 00:09:38,884
每个提示词的第二部分是一个任务。
The second part of every prompt is one task.

108
00:09:39,374 --> 00:09:41,156
准确说明你要构建什么。
State exactly what you're building.

109
00:09:41,648 --> 00:09:45,060
一个功能，一个界面，或者一个集成。
One feature, one screen, one integration.

110
00:09:45,328 --> 00:09:51,140
而不是像“设置 Native wind，构建新手引导界面，并添加身份验证”这种。
Not something like set up native wind and build the onboarding screen and add authentication.

111
00:09:51,726 --> 00:09:56,164
那是把三个提示词合并成一个，因为觉得这样效率高。
That's three prompts merged into one because it felt efficient.

112
00:09:56,494 --> 00:09:58,148
但相信我，其实不然。
But trust me, it isn't.

113
00:09:58,542 --> 00:10:03,780
如果三个任务中有一个出问题了，你根本不知道是哪一个导致的。
If something breaks across three tasks, you can't tell which one caused it.

114
00:10:04,208 --> 00:10:07,908
所以每个提示词只聚焦于一件事。
So stay scoped to one thing per prompt.

115
00:10:08,302 --> 00:10:14,368
每个提示词的第三部分是保护已有功能的约束条件。
The third part of every prompt are constraints that protect what already works.

116
00:10:14,670 --> 00:10:16,928
同样，大多数开发者都会跳过这一步。
And again, most devs skip this.

117
00:10:17,166 --> 00:10:19,716
到目前为止，你构建的每一个功能都是正常的。
Every feature you've built so far is working.

118
00:10:20,048 --> 00:10:25,508
但遗憾的是，除非你说明，否则 AI 不知道要不要动它们。
But unfortunately, the AI doesn't know to leave it alone unless you say so.

119
00:10:26,062 --> 00:10:30,532
所以要加上类似“不要更改界面设计”这样的句子。
So add lines like, do not change the screen design.

120
00:10:30,958 --> 00:10:33,412
“完全保留现有的 UI。”
Preserve the existing UI exactly.

121
00:10:33,838 --> 00:10:40,548
保持现有的 Stream 音频流不变，且不要在移动应用中暴露任何密钥。
Keep the existing stream audio flow intact, and don't expose any secrets in the mobile app.

122
00:10:41,582 --> 00:10:44,900
这些内容告诉 AI 哪些地方不能破坏。
These tell the AI what not to break.

123
00:10:45,422 --> 00:10:54,208
它们是你现有代码的机构记忆，写下来是为了让 AI
把它们当作需要绕过的部分，而不是去重构它们。
They're your working code's institutional memory, written down so the AI treats it as something to work around, not to refactor.

124
00:10:54,414 --> 00:11:01,328
最后，如果涉及视觉内容，每个提示词的第四部分就是设计参考。
And finally, the fourth part of every prompt are design references, if you're doing something visual.

125
00:11:01,614 --> 00:11:05,476
附上那张图片、截图或者设计片段。
Attach that image or screenshot or pieces of the design.

126
00:11:06,030 --> 00:11:11,108
AI 阅读布局的效果比阅读布局描述要好得多。
The AI reads layouts better than it reads descriptions of layouts.

127
00:11:11,470 --> 00:11:16,288
所以一张图片就能省去你解释边距的三次提示词。
So one image will save you three prompts of you explaining margins.

128
00:11:16,448 --> 00:11:20,580
所以综合起来，一个真实的提示词看起来大概是这样的。
So put together, a real prompt looks something like this.

129
00:11:21,166 --> 00:11:24,804
先阅读 AGENTS.md，然后严格遵守它。
Read the agents MD first and then follow it strictly.

130
00:11:25,454 --> 00:11:33,188
按照附带的设计，完全使用 assets 文件夹中的资源来实现新手引导界面。
Implement the onboarding screen as shown in the attached design exactly using the assets from the assets folder.

131
00:11:33,806 --> 00:11:37,924
在主页路由上添加一个导航链接，用于打开新手引导界面。
Add a navigation link on the home route to open up the onboarding screen.

132
00:11:38,158 --> 00:11:42,788
并在应用名称旁边使用吉祥物 Logo 图片作为顶部 Logo。
And use the mascot logo image for the top logo alongside the app name.

133
00:11:43,438 --> 00:11:45,968
不要包含分页点。
Do not include the pagination dots.

134
00:11:46,190 --> 00:11:49,028
然后把图片设计拖进去。
And then also drag and drop the image design.

135
00:11:49,390 --> 00:11:53,732
它很简短，有明确范围，有约束条件，还有参考。
It's short, scoped, has a constraint, and has a reference.

136
00:11:54,158 --> 00:11:59,108
AI 知道该构建什么，不该添加什么，以及它应该长什么样。
The AI knows what to build, what not to add, and what it should look like.

137
00:11:59,566 --> 00:12:14,468
我还准备了一个遵循这些模式的提示词模板，并在下面的免费手册中提供了更多示例，
这样你就可以在任何项目中重复使用它，给你的 AI 提供更多的纪律性和结构。
And I've also prepared a prompt template that follows these patterns alongside more examples in that free playbook down below,
so that you can reuse it across any kind of project to give your AI more discipline and structure.

138
00:12:15,054 --> 00:12:17,124
再次提醒，链接就在下方的描述栏里。
Once again, the link is down in the description.

139
00:12:17,568 --> 00:12:20,708
这就是四部分提示词结构。
And that was the four-part prompt structure.

140
00:12:20,928 --> 00:12:24,196
现在，让我们多聊聊约束条件。
But now, let's talk a bit more about constraints.

141
00:12:24,558 --> 00:12:29,540
即使我教过开发者这种结构，他们还是经常搞错约束条件这一块。
Even when I taught developers the structure, they still got wrong the constraints part.

142
00:12:29,648 --> 00:12:39,408
因为你可以准备好完整的 AGENTS 文件，可以写任务，附上设计，
然后写出一个实际上什么也没限制的约束条件。
Because you can prep the full agents file, you can write the task, attach the design,
and then write a constraint that doesn't actually constrain anything.

143
00:12:39,598 --> 00:12:46,852
这种情况之所以发生，是因为大多数开发者在思考代码时，实际上应该在思考行为。
And that happens because most devs are thinking about code when they should actually be thinking about behavior.

144
00:12:47,598 --> 00:12:52,292
你不需要告诉 AI 如何写代码，它自己会搞定的。
You don't need to tell the AI how to write the code, it'll figure it out.

145
00:12:53,134 --> 00:13:02,980
你需要告诉它的是功能应该如何表现，哪些已经正常运
行且必须保持不变，哪些允许更改，以及哪些是禁区。
What you need to tell it is how the feature should behave, what's already working
that should stay the same, what's allowed to change, and what's off limits.

146
00:13:03,310 --> 00:13:09,380
在后面的构建过程中你会看到一些例子，所以一定要看到最后，它们看起来是这样的。
Some examples that you'll see later on in the build, so definitely make sure to stick until the end, look like this.

147
00:13:09,934 --> 00:13:13,988
如果任何地方不清楚，请在实施之前先提问。
If anything is unclear, ask before implementing.

148
00:13:14,574 --> 00:13:19,492
这可以防止 AI 在遇到歧义时擅自做决定。
That stops the AI from making decisions on its own when it hits ambiguity.

149
00:13:20,398 --> 00:13:24,644
另外，不要在移动应用中暴露任何密钥。
Also, do not expose any secrets in the mobile app.

150
00:13:25,134 --> 00:13:28,228
保持现有的 Stream 音频流不变。
Keep the existing stream audio flow intact.

151
00:13:28,718 --> 00:13:32,644
这能保护安全模型和已经跑通的集成部分。
That protects the security model and the already working integration.

152
00:13:33,742 --> 00:13:39,072
我这些想法就是像产品工程师一样去观察 App 之后想出来的。
And I came up with these just by looking at the app the way that a product engineer would.

153
00:13:39,246 --> 00:13:41,604
从用户的角度来看，可能会出什么问题？
What could go wrong from a user's perspective?

154
00:13:41,792 --> 00:13:45,572
AI 可能会意外修改哪些已经正常运行的部分？
What might the AI accidentally change that's already working?

155
00:13:45,872 --> 00:13:49,668
把这些内容写进提示词的约束条件部分。
Write those things down into the constraint part of the prompt.

156
00:13:49,966 --> 00:13:54,500
好了，现在你已经搞定了这个四部分结构。
Okay, so now you have that four-part structure figured out.

157
00:13:54,832 --> 00:13:58,212
而且你要知道，约束条件必须是关于行为的。
And you know that constraints have to be about behavior.

158
00:13:58,672 --> 00:14:01,284
但并不是每个功能都有设计稿。
But not every feature has a design.

159
00:14:01,838 --> 00:14:06,404
有些是关于状态管理、身份验证逻辑或后端集成的。
Some are about state management, auth logic, or backend integration.

160
00:14:06,926 --> 00:14:10,432
这些没有视觉内容供你添加或拖拽。
There's nothing visual for you to attach or drag and drop.

161
00:14:10,798 --> 00:14:12,868
那该怎么写提示词呢？
So how do you prompt for those?

162
00:14:13,486 --> 00:14:16,612
嗯，同样，只需描述行为即可。
Well, again, just describe behavior.

163
00:14:17,454 --> 00:14:20,868
首先，我们有常规的读取 agents.md 文件并遵循它。
First, we have the usual read agentsmd file and follow it.

164
00:14:21,486 --> 00:14:25,988
然后你告诉它类似「集成语言选择状态」的内容。
Then you tell it something like integrate the language selection state.

165
00:14:26,638 --> 00:14:32,964
使用 Zustand（这是一个状态库）配合 React Native Async storage 来存储选定的语言。
Store the selected language using Zustand, that's a state library, with React Native async storage.

166
00:14:33,166 --> 00:14:35,108
那将是我们首选的数据库。
That's going to be our database of choice.

167
00:14:35,392 --> 00:14:41,476
所以如果已认证用户没有选定的语言，就将他们路由到语言选择页面。
So if an authenticated user has no selected language, route them to the language selection screen.

168
00:14:41,870 --> 00:14:45,956
只有在完成选择后，他们才能到达主页路由。
And then only after the selection should they reach the home route.

169
00:14:46,352 --> 00:14:48,740
完全保留现有的 UI。
Preserve the existing UI exactly.

170
00:14:48,992 --> 00:14:56,228
我们还可以主屏幕上加一个临时按钮来清除 Async storage，这样我才能实际测试这个流程。
And we can also add a temporary button on the home screen to clear the async storage so I can actually test the flow.

171
00:14:56,494 --> 00:15:01,028
第一部分是关于我们希望用户如何使用 App 的行为。
The first part is the behavior of how we want our users to be able to use the app.

172
00:15:01,152 --> 00:15:05,540
而最后那行是开发工具，你稍后会把它删掉。
And that last line is a development utility that you'll remove later.

173
00:15:05,806 --> 00:15:12,548
所以记住，要为让你能验证功能的底层架构写提示词，而不仅仅是功能本身。
So remember, prompt for the infrastructure that lets you verify the feature, not just the feature itself.

174
00:15:15,054 --> 00:15:19,300
那如果 AI 本身就是问题所在呢？
And what about cases where the AI itself is the problem?

175
00:15:19,952 --> 00:15:23,844
比如它根本不知道你正在使用的东西的当前版本。
Where it just doesn't know the current version of the thing you're using.

176
00:15:24,654 --> 00:15:28,996
这在更新频繁的库和服务中非常常见。
This is incredibly common with libraries and services that update fast.

177
00:15:29,582 --> 00:15:33,668
AI 的训练数据可能落后好几个月，有时甚至是一年。
The AI's training data is months behind, sometimes a year.

178
00:15:33,998 --> 00:15:43,876
所以它生成的代码看起来是对的，但它使用了弃用方法、旧的 API，
或者是在上一个大版本中刚刚改变的配置模式。
So it generates code that looks right, but it uses a deprecated method, an old API,
or a config pattern that just changed in the last major version.

179
00:15:44,206 --> 00:15:49,668
除非在构建时或生产环境中出问题，否则你根本不会注意到这些变化。
You won't notice these changes until something breaks at build time or in production.

180
00:15:50,382 --> 00:15:52,612
幸运的是，修复方法很简单。
And the fix, thankfully, is simple.

181
00:15:53,134 --> 00:16:00,612
只需在指令后面直接粘贴当前的文档，中间用分隔符隔开即可。
Just paste the current documentation directly into the prompt after the instructions, separated by a divider.

182
00:16:01,582 --> 00:16:08,228
举个例子，就像是：用真实的 Clerk 身份验证替换模拟的身份验证流程。
An example would be something like replace the mocked auth flow with real clerk authentication.

183
00:16:08,686 --> 00:16:11,712
保持现有的 UI 和导航不变。
Keep the existing UI and navigation intact.

184
00:16:12,110 --> 00:16:20,452
通过 Clerk 实现邮件注册、登录、社交认证和验证，验证通过后跳转到主页路由。
Implement email signup, sign-in, social auth, and verification through clerk, and then after verification, navigate to the home route.

185
00:16:21,038 --> 00:16:27,748
然后，只需把从他们官网上复制下来的 Clerk Markdown 文档粘贴进去就行了。
And then after all of that, simply paste the markdown clerk docs, which you can copy over from their website.

186
00:16:28,032 --> 00:16:39,172
这样一来，AI 会先阅读你的指令，理解你想构建什么，
然后再利用文档用最新版本的 API 来正确完成任务。
That way, the AI will read your instructions first, understand what you're trying to build,
and then use the docs to do it correctly with the latest version of the API.

187
00:16:39,758 --> 00:16:45,124
对于任何你不确定 AI 是否掌握最新版本的库，都可以这样做。
And you can do this for any library where you're not sure whether the AI has the current version.

188
00:16:45,358 --> 00:16:50,192
此外，对于发布官方智能体技能包的库，还有更简洁的路径。
And there's also a cleaner path for libraries that publish official skill packs.

189
00:16:50,432 --> 00:16:52,836
现在几乎所有的开发工具都有这种功能。
And almost every dev tool nowadays does that.

190
00:16:53,262 --> 00:17:02,272
你只需要安装一次智能体技能，然后 AI 就会自动使用正确的版本，不需要你每次都粘贴文档。
You simply need to install the agent skill once, and then the AI will keep using
the right version automatically without you needing to paste the docs every time.

191
00:17:02,512 --> 00:17:05,310
Expo、Clerk 和 Stream 都有这些技能。
Expo, Clerk, and Stream all have them.

192
00:17:05,550 --> 00:17:10,276
稍后我会教大家如何为你们使用的任何工具安装这些智能体技能。
And I'll teach you later on how we can install those agent skills for any tool you're using.

193
00:17:10,512 --> 00:17:18,980
另一个选择是使用类似 Context7 的工具，它也能为你使用的任何工具带入最新的文档。
Another option as well is to use something like Context7, which also
brings back the latest version of documentations for any tool you're using.

194
00:17:19,374 --> 00:17:27,460
但再次强调，如果你一直看到视频最后，我会教你如何在实践中运用所有这些方法，
确保你的智能体始终拥有最新信息。
But again, if you stick along throughout this video, I'll teach you how to use all
of those in practice to make sure that your agents always have the latest info.

195
00:17:27,694 --> 00:17:37,312
