access it first and at the most affordable price.

198
00:17:55,502 --> 00:17:58,240
我会在描述栏留下链接，方便你加入候补名单。
I'll leave the link down in the description so you can join the wait list.

199
00:17:58,574 --> 00:18:04,228
现在让我多聊聊当你的应用程序出现故障时该如何写提示词。
And now let me tell you a bit more about how to prompt when something in your application breaks.

200
00:18:04,526 --> 00:18:09,380
我的意思是，即使用了我给你的这种完整结构，有时还是会出问题的。
I mean, even with this full structure that I'm giving you, things will break sometimes.

201
00:18:10,158 --> 00:18:11,940
这不是方法的失败。
That's not a failure of the method.

202
00:18:12,270 --> 00:18:14,084
这就是软件开发的常态。
It's just how software development is.

203
00:18:14,766 --> 00:18:18,660
所以当出问题时，应对方法始终如一。
So when something breaks, the response is always the same.

204
00:18:19,120 --> 00:18:22,480
只需写一个针对性的修复提示词。
Write just one targeted prompt fix.

205
00:18:22,720 --> 00:18:27,940
比如：验证模型在 iOS 上出现在键盘后面。
Something like the verification model is appearing behind the keyboard on iOS.

206
00:18:28,494 --> 00:18:30,180
它应该显示在键盘上方。
It should sit above the keyboard.

207
00:18:30,542 --> 00:18:33,796
不要更改任何其他模型的行为或布局。
Don't change any other model behavior or layout.

208
00:18:34,542 --> 00:18:36,548
你不需要重新解释功能。
You don't need to re-explain the feature.

209
00:18:36,878 --> 00:18:47,012
你不需要粘贴整个代码库，只需陈述问题，说明正确的行为，
然后在必要时添加约束条件，以确保其他内容保持不变。
You don't paste the code base, you state the problem, state the correct behavior,
and then add a constraint if needed to keep everything else untouched.

210
00:18:47,200 --> 00:18:51,748
这意味着：一个问题，一个修复，一次验证。
So this means one problem, one fix, and one verification.

211
00:18:52,302 --> 00:18:53,348
就这样。
And that's it.

212
00:18:53,710 --> 00:18:55,556
这就是如何写好提示词。
That's how you can prompt well.

213
00:18:56,398 --> 00:19:01,440
最后，让我用一句话把这一切串联起来。
So finally, let me give you one sentence that ties all of it together.

214
00:19:01,710 --> 00:19:06,820
完美的提示词就是带有明确范围的指令。
A perfect prompt is just an instruction with a defined scope.

215
00:19:07,630 --> 00:19:09,508
而这个范围包含三件事。
And the scope is three things.

216
00:19:09,934 --> 00:19:11,280
你现在正在构建什么？
What are you building right now?

217
00:19:11,520 --> 00:19:17,412
哪些部分是不动手的，以及 AI 已经从文件中知道哪些规则。
What are the works that you're not touching, and what rules the AI already knows from the file.

218
00:19:18,222 --> 00:19:22,212
一旦确定了这三点，提示词几乎就是自动生成的。
Once those three are decided, the prompt almost writes itself.

219
00:19:22,830 --> 00:19:29,796
agents.md 处理规则，任务行处理新内容，约束条件处理受保护的内容。
AgentsMD handles the rules, the task line handles what's new, and the constraints handle what's protected.

220
00:19:30,190 --> 00:19:34,500
如果需要，你最终还可以添加设计参考或粘贴文档。
And you can eventually add a design reference or a doc paste if needed.

221
00:19:34,926 --> 00:19:35,492
就是这样。
That's it.

222
00:19:36,110 --> 00:19:39,908
所以先构建新手引导界面，看看是否正常，然后继续。
So build the onboarding screen, see if it works, move on.

223
00:19:40,334 --> 00:19:45,028
登录界面、语言选择以及后续的所有功能也一样。
Same for the sign-in, the language selection, and every other feature to follow.

224
00:19:45,582 --> 00:19:50,276
这样当某些东西出问题时，影响是可控的，因为你只改动了一件事。
And then when something breaks, it's contained because you only changed one thing.

225
00:19:51,022 --> 00:19:57,732
如果你按照我稍后在构建过程中会展示的方法来构建，你下次可以把它应用到任何其他项目上。
If you build this way, which I'm going to show you how to do later on in the build, you can apply it to anything else next.

226
00:19:58,030 --> 00:20:01,520
产品会变，但工作流不会变。
The product will change, but the workflow doesn't.

227
00:20:01,760 --> 00:20:03,140
这才是真正的核心技能。
That's the actual skill.

228
00:20:03,566 --> 00:20:07,396
这也是你看到视频结束时能带走的收获。
And that's what you're walking away from watching this video until the end.

229
00:20:07,630 --> 00:20:11,428
你在这里学到的工作流适用于任何技术栈。
The workflow that you'll learn here runs on any stack.

230
00:20:11,982 --> 00:20:14,400
但这是我们这次构建中使用的技术栈。
But here's the one that we're using for this build.

231
00:20:14,560 --> 00:20:15,780
那我们开始设置吧。
So let's get it set up.

232
00:20:16,046 --> 00:20:19,600
对于身份验证和用户管理，我们将使用 Clerk。
For authentication and user management, we'll use Clerk.

233
00:20:20,014 --> 00:20:29,316
说实话，React Native 和 Expo 的开发者体验非常出色，
尤其是在处理 OTP 身份验证、会话和受保护路由方面。
The developer experience for React Native and Expo is honestly really clean, especially for OTP auth, sessions, and protected routes.

234
00:20:29,678 --> 00:20:33,444
你可以完全自定义，也可以启用他们预构建的组件。
